  "intent": "The site is one static page, index.html, in the repository root, with no build step\nand no JavaScript. All of its CSS is in one inline <style> block in the <head>:\n`html, body` use flexbox (display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\nheight: 100%; margin: 0) to center the content on a dark slate background (#0f172a),\nwith the font stack -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif.\nThe h1 is #f8fafc, 3rem, weight 600. The <head> holds <!DOCTYPE html>, <html lang=\"en\">,\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">, the viewport meta, a <title>, and two relative favicon links\n(favicon.ico with sizes=\"32x32\", favicon.svg with type=\"image/svg+xml\").\nStyle: HTML elements are not indented (all at column 0); only the CSS inside <style>\nis indented, 2 spaces per level. Double-quoted attributes, no self-closing slash on\nvoid elements, LF line endings with a final newline.\nThe site is deployed to GitHub Pages under the /test-project/ subpath, so every link\nand asset path must be relative (contact.html, not /contact.html).\n.github/workflows/deploy.yml publishes only the files named on its \"cp ... _site/\" line.\nDo not push, do not open a pull request, and do not touch files outside your task's list.\n\nCreate the contact page\n\nCreate contact.html in the repository root, matching index.html's style exactly: copy\nits <head> (same doctype, lang, charset, viewport, the two favicon links with their\ncomment, and the same inline <style> block), with the title \"Contact\". The body holds,\nunindented: <h1>Contact</h1>, one short paragraph saying questions go to the GitHub\nrepository's issues, and a link back to the home page with href=\"index.html\".\nBecause the body is a flex row, add to the <style> block `flex-direction: column;` on\n`html, body` so the heading, paragraph and link stack vertically, plus a `p, a` rule\n(or similar) giving them color #f8fafc so they read on the dark background; keep the\n2-space CSS indentation.\nIn .github/workflows/deploy.yml, change the staging line\n`cp index.html favicon.ico favicon.svg _site/` to\n`cp index.html contact.html favicon.ico favicon.svg _site/` so the page is published.\nCommit your work.\n\nThe files this task changes: contact.html, .github/workflows/deploy.yml\n\nCheck your work with: grep -q '<h1>Contact</h1>' contact.html && grep -q 'href=\"index.html\"' contact.html && grep -q 'issues' contact.html && grep -q 'cp index.html contact.html' .github/workflows/deploy.yml\n\nYou are a subagent: another agent started you for this one task and reads your last reply as its result. Commit your work to your branch and publish nothing: no push, no pull request. Nobody will answer a question: decide yourself, and say in your last reply what you did and what you decided.",
